From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:55:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/29] acpi: Don't point to coreboot's TPM2 log when edk2
 publishes one

edk2 imports coreboot's TPM 2.0 event log from CBMEM and publishes a
complete log, covering coreboot's and its own measurements, through
the EFI configuration table. Linux reads the log from the ACPI TPM2
table first, so as long as the table points to coreboot's log the OS
never sees the measurements made by edk2.

Leave LAML/LASA empty when edk2 has its TPM drivers. Unlike Dasharo's
change ("acpi: don't publish TPM logs if EDK payload is used"), keep
the TPM2 table itself, because the edk2 UefiPayloadPkg uses it to
detect the TPM.

Link: https://github.com/Dasharo/coreboot/commit/a183145fa047b7677cb8a49112bab336f4b91fdb
Signed-off-by: Deividas Nastajus <16858119+dns54@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/acpi/acpi.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/acpi/acpi.c b/src/acpi/acpi.c
index 155105b96d..8ddb7048e9 100644
--- a/src/acpi/acpi.c
+++ b/src/acpi/acpi.c
@@ -289,8 +289,15 @@ static void acpi_create_tpm2(acpi_header_t *header, void *unused)
 	/*
 	 * Some payloads like SeaBIOS depend on log area to use TPM2.
 	 * Get the memory size and address of TPM2 log area or initialize it.
+	 *
+	 * edk2 publishes a complete log that includes coreboot's, and the OS
+	 * reads this table's log first, so leave it out. Keep the table: edk2
+	 * uses it to detect the TPM.
 	 */
-	void *lasa = get_tpm2_log(&tpm2_log_len);
+	void *lasa = NULL;
+	tpm2_log_len = 0;
+	if (!CONFIG(PAYLOAD_EDK2) || CONFIG(EDK2_DISABLE_TPM))
+		lasa = get_tpm2_log(&tpm2_log_len);
 	if (!lasa)
 		tpm2_log_len = 0;
 
